Third-party code

rind copies code from the projects below. Each copied file keeps its
source's copyright lines and names its license in an
SPDX-License-Identifier comment. The license texts follow this list.
ALGORITHMS.md's Sources table names the same projects: a change that copies
code from a new project updates both.

Graviola <https://github.com/ctz/graviola>

  What: rind began as a copy of Graviola, and rind-rustls as a copy of
  its rustls-graviola. Files Graviola wrote carry a "Written for
  Graviola by ..." header. Its aarch64 ChaCha20 and its Poly1305 began
  as cifra <https://github.com/ctz/cifra>, by the same author under
  CC0-1.0.
  Copyright 2024 Joe Birr-Pixton
  License: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT-0, the same choice as rind's own code.
  Graviola has no NOTICE file.

s2n-bignum <https://github.com/awslabs/s2n-bignum>

  What: the files under rind/src/low/x86_64 and rind/src/low/aarch64
  that begin "generated source. do not edit.", which admin/parse-asm
  transliterates from s2n-bignum's assembly.
  Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
  License: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT-0, except for:

  - The ML-KEM routines (mlkem_*.rs) and the aarch64 Keccak-f routines
    (sha3_keccak_f1600.rs, sha3_keccak_f1600_alt.rs,
    sha3_keccak2_f1600.rs), which s2n-bignum takes from mlkem-native
    <https://github.com/pq-code-package/mlkem-native>.
    License: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT. Further copyright lines:
      Copyright (c) 2024 The mlkem-native project authors
      Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Arm Limited
      Copyright (c) 2022 Arm Limited
      Copyright (c) 2022 Hanno Becker
      Copyright (c) 2022 Matthias Kannwischer
      Copyright (c) 2023 Amin Abdulrahman, Matthias Kannwischer

  - The x86_64 Keccak-f routine (x86_64/sha3_keccak_f1600.rs), which
    s2n-bignum takes from OpenSSL <https://github.com/openssl/openssl>,
    written by Andy Polyakov.
    License: Apache-2.0. Further copyright line:
      Copyright (c) 2017-2024 The OpenSSL Project Authors

  s2n-bignum's NOTICE file reads:
    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.

libcrux <https://github.com/cryspen/libcrux>

  What: rind/src/low/arm/aes.rs, the bitsliced AES block cipher and key
  expansion from libcrux-aes 0.0.10.
  Copyright 2023 Cryspen Sarl
  License: Apache-2.0. libcrux has no NOTICE file.

HACL* <https://github.com/hacl-star/hacl-star>, through libcrux

  What: rind/src/low/arm/chacha20.rs, the ChaCha20 block function that
  libcrux-chacha20poly1305 0.0.10 compiles from HACL*'s Hacl_Chacha20.
  Copyright (c) 2016-2022 INRIA, CMU and Microsoft Corporation
  Copyright (c) 2022-2023 HACL* Contributors
  Copyright 2023 Cryspen Sarl
  License: Apache-2.0. Neither project has a NOTICE file.

HACL* <https://github.com/hacl-star/hacl-star>, Vale

  What: the files under rind/src/low/x86_64/hacl, Vale's x86_64 AES-GCM,
  which admin/import-hacl takes from HACL*'s dist/vale at commit
  f557259007db9933442dde10aa995c1b00bd3446. Its gcm*_opt routines port
  OpenSSL's aesni-gcm-x86_64, which OpenSSL releases under Apache-2.0.
  Copyright (c) 2016-2022 INRIA, CMU and Microsoft Corporation
  Copyright (c) 2022-2023 HACL* Contributors
  Copyright 2013-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors
  License: Apache-2.0. HACL* has no NOTICE file.

aws-lc <https://github.com/aws/aws-lc>, from OpenSSL and BoringSSL

  What: the files under rind/src/low/{arm,aarch64,x86_64}/aws_lc but
  the mlkem_* ones (see mlkem-native), which
  admin/import-aws-lc takes from aws-lc's assembly at commit
  91c93a8eb860e51482a871a8772cb9b1b310baea,
  rind/src/low/arm/poly1305_arm.rs,
  rind/src/low/x86_64/ghash_ssse3_x86_64.rs,
  rind/src/low/x86_64/rsaz.rs, rind/src/low/x86_64/aes_nohw.rs, and
  rind/src/low/generic/ghash_nohw.rs:

  - For 32-bit ARM, aesv8-armx.s (AES), ghashv8-armx.s (GHASH),
    sha1-armv4-large.s (SHA1), sha256-armv4.s (SHA256), sha512-armv4.s
    (SHA512), and chacha-armv4.s (ChaCha20); for aarch64 and x86_64, the
    sha512_block_data_order_* routines and the K512 tables of
    sha512-armv8 and sha512-x86_64 (SHA512); for x86_64, the
    sha256_block_data_order_avx, _ssse3, and _nohw routines and the K256
    table of sha256-x86_64 (SHA256), the sha1_block_data_order_avx,
    _ssse3, and _nohw routines and the K_XX_XX table of sha1-x86_64
    (SHA1), and the
    ChaCha20_ctr32_nohw and _ssse3_4x routines and tables of chacha-x86_64
    (ChaCha20); the bn_mul_mont_nohw, bn_mul4x_mont, bn_mulx4x_mont, and
    bn_sqr8x_mont routines of x86_64-mont and bn_sqr8x_internal and
    bn_sqrx8x_internal of x86_64-mont5, and the rsaz_1024_*
    routines and tables of rsaz-avx2 (RSA); the
    aes_hw_ctr32_encrypt_blocks and aes_hw_cbc_encrypt routines of
    aesni-x86_64 (AES-CTR and AES-CBC), the
    vpaes_* routines and table of vpaes-x86_64 (AES), and the
    ecp_nistz256_* routines and tables of p256-x86_64-asm (P-256); for
    aarch64, the bn_mul_mont routine of armv8-mont (RSA), the vpaes_*
    routines and table of vpaes-armv8 (AES), the gcm_*_neon routines and
    table of ghash-neon-armv8 (GHASH), and the *_block_data_order_nohw
    routines and table of sha1-armv8 (SHA1) and sha256-armv8 (SHA256). All
    are pregenerated from Perl scripts written for OpenSSL by Andy Polyakov,
    or for rsaz-avx2 and p256-x86_64-asm by Shay Gueron and Vlad Krasnov
    of Intel, which Andy Polyakov extended for p256-x86_64-asm;
    vpaes-armv8 and vpaes-x86_64 adapt the public domain vector permutation
    AES by Mike Hamburg. ghash_ssse3_x86_64.rs ports aws-lc's
    gcm_init_ssse3, from crypto/fipsmodule/modes/gcm.c, to Rust, and
    rsaz.rs its RSAZ_1024_mod_exp_avx2, from crypto/fipsmodule/bn/rsaz_exp.c.
    Copyright (c) 2008 The OpenSSL Project. All rights reserved.
    Copyright 2005-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2006-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2007-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2009-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2010-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2011-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2013-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2014-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2014-2020 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2015-2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright 2016 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright (c) 2012, Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright (c) 2014, Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.
    Copyright (c) 2015 CloudFlare, Inc.
    License: Apache-2.0.

  - poly1305_arm_asm.s (Poly1305 with NEON), and poly1305_arm.rs, which
    ports aws-lc's crypto/poly1305/poly1305_arm.c to Rust. BoringSSL took
    both from the public domain neon2 version in SUPERCOP by D. J.
    Bernstein and Peter Schwabe.
    Copyright (c) 2014, Google Inc.
    License: ISC.

  - For x86_64 and aarch64, the chacha20_poly1305_open and _seal
    routines, the poly_hash_ad_internal helper, and the tables of
    chacha20_poly1305_x86_64 and chacha20_poly1305_armv8
    (ChaCha20-Poly1305), which aws-lc takes from BoringSSL. Both are
    pregenerated from Perl scripts written by Vlad Krasnov.
    Copyright (c) 2015, CloudFlare Ltd.
    Copyright (c) 2020, CloudFlare Ltd.
    License: ISC.

  - For x86_64, the gcm_ghash_ssse3 routine and tables of
    ghash-ssse3-x86_64 (GHASH), which aws-lc takes from BoringSSL;
    aes_nohw.rs, which ports aws-lc's crypto/fipsmodule/aes/aes_nohw.c
    (AES), in its SSE2 configuration, to Rust; and, for x86_64 and 32-bit ARM, ghash_nohw.rs, which ports aws-lc's
    crypto/fipsmodule/modes/gcm_nohw.c (GHASH) to Rust. aws-lc takes both
    C files from BoringSSL.
    Copyright (c) 2019, Google Inc.
    License: ISC.

  aws-lc's NOTICE file reads:
    AWS-LC
    Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.

mlkem-native <https://github.com/pq-code-package/mlkem-native>

  What: rind/src/low/generic/mlkem_poly.rs, which ports mlkem-native's
  portable C polynomial arithmetic (mlkem/poly.c, poly_k.c, compress.c,
  sampling.c, and zetas.inc, as aws-lc vendors them at commit
  91c93a8eb860e51482a871a8772cb9b1b310baea) to Rust; and
  rind/src/low/x86_64/aws_lc/mlkem_*, which admin/import-aws-lc takes from
  mlkem-native's x86_64 AVX2 assembly as aws-lc vendors it at that commit,
  with the tables of its compress_consts.c in
  rind/src/low/x86_64/mlkem_compress.rs.
  Copyright (c) The mlkem-native project authors
  License: Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT.

BoringSSL <https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl>

  What: the files under rind/src/low/{x86_64,arm}/boringssl, which
  admin/import-boringssl takes from BoringSSL at commit
  ed9209cff8b5a2fbc6c10050f29b3355048bda85: for x86_64, AES-GCM on VAES
  from its pregenerated gen/bcm/aes-gcm-avx2-x86_64 and
  aes-gcm-avx512-x86_64, the AVX-512 one based on aes-gcm-avx10-x86_64.S
  from Linux; for 32-bit ARM, X25519 on NEON from
  crypto/curve25519/asm/x25519-asm-arm.S, which BoringSSL took from
  crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/neon2/scalarmult.s in SUPERCOP 20141124
  <https://bench.cr.yp.to/supercop.html>, which is public domain.
  Copyright 2015 The BoringSSL Authors
  Copyright 2024 The BoringSSL Authors
  License: Apache-2.0. BoringSSL has no NOTICE file.

OpenSSL <https://github.com/openssl/openssl>

  What: the files under rind/src/low/{x86_64,arm}/openssl, which
  admin/import-openssl takes from OpenSSL at commit
  2f4e3a5fec05394068cfa7379890ab552483a8a6: for x86_64, SHA-256 and
  SHA-512 on AVX2 and SHA-512 on the SHA512 instructions, generated from
  crypto/sha/asm/sha512-x86_64.pl, written by Andy Polyakov;
  for 32-bit ARM, Keccak-f[1600] in integer code and on NEON, generated from
  crypto/sha/asm/keccak1600-armv4.pl, written by Andy Polyakov.
  Copyright 2005-2026 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
  Copyright 2017-2026 The OpenSSL Project Authors. All Rights Reserved.
  License: Apache-2.0. OpenSSL has no NOTICE file.

curve25519-dalek <https://github.com/dalek-cryptography/curve25519-dalek>

  What: rind/src/low/x86_64/edwards25519_scalarmuldouble_avx2.rs, a port
  of curve25519-dalek 5.0.0's AVX2 backend (its field arithmetic, point
  formulas, and table of the base point's odd multiples) and its scalars'
  non-adjacent forms, for Ed25519 verification on x86_64 CPUs with AVX2 but
  without ADX.
  Copyright (c) 2016-2021 isis agora lovecruft. All rights reserved.
  Copyright (c) 2016-2021 Henry de Valence. All rights reserved.
  License: BSD-3-Clause.

